{
  "_comment": "APP MODE (plan row 0e). ComfyUI's app view shows a workflow as a form: extra.linearData.inputs is the form, top to bottom, in exactly this order (the frontend does not sort it), and extra.linearMode opens the workflow straight into it. ONE FORM FOR EVERY GENERATED WORKFLOW, in the operator's order (the operator, 2026-09-26, after using the form: \"language, size, acts, story bank, visual style, video model, TTS model, music model, story writing models including cloud sub options, upscaler, my story fields\"): language, cast size, acts, the story bank with its source-to-adapt row, visual style, the three video pickers each with its still under it, the two voice pickers, the music composer, the two writers and the six cloud writer slots, the upscaler; then the one row he did not list (Lemmy cameo; the story idea and episode title rows were taken off the form by the operator on 2026-09-28 -- both widgets stay on the canvas, blank by default); then the My Story rows and Space saver; then every checklist -- the language, bank, style, video-lane and still-model pools -- at the foot (operator, 2026-09-28: the clickbox sections go at the bottom after Space saver), with the Yes/No model-roll switches above the pickers they replace. Wording and grouping from a Fable design pass the operator asked for; the form has no section headers, so the role prefixes in `labels` do that job. Per-machine workflows OPEN ON THE GRAPH (operator: graph view) and switch to the form with the App button; workflows/otr_app.json opens as the app. scripts/build_variants.py resolves each entry's node TYPE and widget against the workflow's own node ids and refuses a type that is missing or not unique, or a widget that node does not have. The canonical carries neither: it is the workflow the operator edits on the canvas. HAND-ORDERED ON PURPOSE -- the matrix's key_indicators omit the cloud slots and include machine tuning; tests/test_app_mode.py checks no matrix user-choice key is missing. `labels` gives each row a plain-English name, written as the widget input's `label` on the generated workflows only. REWORDED 2026-10-23 after a design round read as a first-time user (Opus, briefed to refute): the form must say when a row is ignored -- My Story needs the my_story bank, the still rows are unused by a video lane that takes no still, a Randomize switch overrides the pickers under it, a cloud slot needs a Writer set to it, each checklist is read only by its own roll -- and what a setting costs (a paid composer, a slower upscale). Dropdown VALUES stay the pack's ids: App Mode shows the raw id even with locale option labels (measured on frontend 1.55.18), so the label and the one help line carry everything. QA FOLD, same day (Sonnet, briefed to refute): a help line states only what the code does -- the credits card prints the style on every lane, three AnimateDiff lanes take no still without saying so in the dropdown, Japanese and Mandarin voices need libraries a 3.12 box installs by hand, an id in Source needs a named bank, and an empty checklist is the whole list.",
